{"name":"Sehnsucht Red","hex":"#903037","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sehnsucht","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Sehnsucht."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sehnsucht"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sehnsucht","blocks":[{"text":"Sehnsucht is a German noun translated as \"longing\", \"desire\", \"yearning\", or \"craving\". Some psychologists use the word to represent thoughts and feelings about all facets of life that are unfinished or imperfect, paired with a yearning for ideal alternative experiences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Sehnsucht_%281895%29%2C_oil_painting_by_Oskar_Zwintscher_%281870-1916%29.jpg/330px-Sehnsucht_%281895%29%2C_oil_painting_by_Oskar_Zwintscher_%281870-1916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sehnsucht"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Heinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_%28Tr%C3%A4umerei%29_c1900.jpg/500px-Heinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_%28Tr%C3%A4umerei%29_c1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Heinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_%28Tr%C3%A4umerei%29_c1900.jpg/1280px-Heinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_%28Tr%C3%A4umerei%29_c1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Heinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_%28Tr%C3%A4umerei%29_c1900.jpg/500px-Heinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_%28Tr%C3%A4umerei%29_c1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sehnsucht (Dreaming) by Heinrich Vogeler about 1900","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeinrich_Vogeler_Sehnsucht_(Tr%C3%A4umerei)_c1900.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Sehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg/500px-Sehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Sehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg/1280px-Sehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Sehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg/500px-Sehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sehnsucht, sculpture by Susanne Kraißer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASehnsucht_Susanne_Krai%C3%9Fer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.w